+# Multirole Carrier Families, Mission Profiles, and World Adaptation Atlas
+
+## Design Correction
+
+The named carrier concepts below are not exclusive ship classes.
+
+Each is a broad-spectrum carrier civilization with a recognizable **design lineage and customary emphasis**. Individual builds may reverse, blend or abandon that emphasis.
+
+A carrier family must remain capable of habitation, care, repair, fabrication, logistics, deployment, governance, culture, rescue and defense unless the story explicitly concerns a damaged, incomplete or exploitative vessel.
+
+# 1. Shared Family Matrix
+
+| Family | Customary emphasis | Strong secondary roles | Common carried bases |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Hearth Convoy | habitation and migration | repair, trade, care, survey | crawlers, flotilla homes, clinics, aerostats |
+| Atlas Gate Tender | route construction | fabrication, survey, rescue, trade | anchor craft, tugs, construction carriers, labs |
+| Ocean Bastion | ocean interface | ecology, settlement, rescue, trade | submarines, flotillas, amphibious crawlers, seafloor habitats |
+| Foundry Forge | heavy fabrication | logistics, settlement, salvage, repair | mining crawlers, yards, haulers, workshops |
+| Sanctuary Mercy | care and refuge | logistics, fabrication, diplomacy, evacuation | clinics, medevac, shelters, water plants |
+| Frontier Survey | exploration | science, settlement, care, fabrication | landers, labs, aerostats, rovers, drones |
+| Bastion Escort | convoy security | rescue, logistics, repair, command | escorts, evacuation craft, clinics, barriers |
+| Carnival Exchange | trade and culture | diplomacy, fabrication, care, education | market shuttles, stages, guest habitats, workshops |
+| Night Burrow | hostile-world endurance | survey, care, fabrication, defense | burrowers, walkers, shelters, hardened labs |
+| Seed Ark | continuity and founding | ecology, education, fabrication, diplomacy | settlement carriers, archives, nurseries, mobile homes |
+
+None of these names defines a universal faction or fixed model.
+
+# 2. Hearth Convoy Carrier
+
+## Character
+
+A moving neighborhood and logistics parent for independent mobile homes.
+
+## Multirole baseline
+
+- machine shops and parts production;
+- regional clinic and quarantine;
+- survey and navigation department;
+- cargo and trade decks;
+- schools and public assembly;
+- rescue craft;
+- defensive hardening;
+- ecological and food systems.
+
+## Common variants
+
+### Public migration carrier
+
+Carries displaced households and municipal services under a public charter.
+
+### Cooperative road-to-orbit carrier
+
+Owned by vehicle crews and settlements connected through recurring routes.
+
+### Prestige house carrier
+
+Highly comfortable and politically influential, but still dependent on public docks and independent crews.
+
+### Sparse frontier carrier
+
+Fewer permanent residents, more deployment and fabrication capacity.
+
+## Gameplay
+
+- convoy formation;
+- household politics;
+- arrival at settlements;
+- refitting carried mobile homes;
+- rescue and migration;
+- trade routes;
+- preserving old vehicles inside a changing ship.
+
+# 3. Atlas Gate Tender
+
+## Character
+
+A mobile route-engineering city that builds, inspects and repairs metric infrastructure.
+
+## Multirole baseline
+
+It still supports ordinary habitation, clinics, gardens, schools, trade, rescue, defense and planetary deployment.
+
+## Variants
+
+### Anchor-laying tender
+
+Large deployment bays and deep reserves.
+
+### Corridor survey tender
+
+More sensing, science and diplomacy.
+
+### Route-repair community
+
+A long-lived traveling workforce with extensive family districts.
+
+### Independent standards carrier
+
+Maintains interoperability and certification across hostile political borders.
+
+## Gameplay
+
+- surveying candidate routes;
+- carrying construction bases;
+- negotiating passage;
+- repairing anchors;
+- rescue after corridor failure;
+- hosting rival standards delegations;
+- deciding whether route access should be public, private or restricted.
+
+# 4. Ocean Bastion Carrier
+
+## Character
+
+A spacecraft, atmospheric interface vessel and mobile maritime civilization capable of supporting surface and deep-ocean operations.
+
+## Multirole baseline
+
+- orbital and marine fabrication;
+- hospitals and pressure medicine;
+- gardens and aquaculture;
+- cargo and trade;
+- science;
+- habitat deployment;
+- search and rescue;
+- defense and storm shelter;
+- schools and maritime law.
+
+## Carried bases
+
+- expedition submarines;
+- flotilla homes;
+- seafloor habitats;
+- amphibious crawlers;
+- dive bells;
+- marine drones;
+- floating workshops.
+
+## Variants
+
+### Warm-sea settlement carrier
+
+Optimized for flotilla founding, aquaculture and trade.
+
+### Ice-ocean penetrator carrier
+
+Carries drilling, melting, subglacial and radiation systems.
+
+### Abyssal science and rescue carrier
+
+Deep-pressure capacity, care and heavy recovery.
+
+### Naval commons carrier
+
+Protects civilian shipping while operating courts, repair and relief services.
+
+## Gameplay
+
+- orbital-to-ocean deployment;
+- storms and currents;
+- submarine expeditions;
+- floating settlement politics;
+- marine ecological work;
+- naval logistics and rescue;
+- first contact with oceanic civilizations.
+
+# 5. Foundry Forge Carrier
+
+## Character
+
+A mobile industrial district capable of building infrastructure, modules and smaller vessels.
+
+## Multirole baseline
+
+Even the heaviest forge includes homes, clinics, gardens, schools, rescue systems, survey capacity, governance and cultural life.
+
+## Variants
+
+### Asteroid foundry
+
+Local metal and shielding, limited planetary interface.
+
+### Reconstruction carrier
+
+Deploys workshops and public infrastructure after disaster.
+
+### Independent shipyard carrier
+
+Builds and refits craft while moving between settlements.
+
+### Salvage coalition carrier
+
+Uses mixed standards and has unusually visible historical layers.
+
+## Gameplay
+
+- industrial supply chains;
+- yard expansion;
+- salvage ethics;
+- labor and safety;
+- building mobile bases;
+- repairing other carriers;
+- deciding what civilization should be built with finite capacity.
+
+# 6. Sanctuary Mercy Carrier
+
+## Character
+
+A humanitarian carrier whose customary allocation favors care, refuge and recovery.
+
+## Multirole baseline
+
+It also carries:
+
+- substantial fabrication;
+- water and food systems;
+- survey and assessment craft;
+- cargo logistics;
+- diplomatic quarters;
+- evacuation and planetary bases;
+- proportionate defense;
+- education and long-term settlement support.
+
+## Variants
+
+### Rapid disaster carrier
+
+More deployment, triage and logistics.
+
+### Recovery neighborhood carrier
+
+Long rehabilitation, families and education.
+
+### Quarantine and contact carrier
+
+Biological isolation, diplomacy and science.
+
+### Reconstruction trust carrier
+
+Care combined with public works and legal support.
+
+## Gameplay
+
+- disaster assessment;
+- medical and logistical triage;
+- refuge governance;
+- quarantine under uncertainty;
+- reconstruction;
+- neutral access negotiations;
+- resisting political capture of aid.
+
+# 7. Frontier Survey Carrier
+
+## Character
+
+A mobile university, expedition harbor and settlement precursor.
+
+## Multirole baseline
+
+It retains fabrication, habitation, care, cargo, governance, education, emergency shelter, defense and trade.
+
+## Variants
+
+### Planetary survey carrier
+
+More landers, atmospheric systems and ecology labs.
+
+### Deep-space observatory carrier
+
+More sensing, quiet systems and long-duration autonomy.
+
+### First-contact survey carrier
+
+Translation, quarantine, diplomacy and noninterference capability.
+
+### Community science carrier
+
+Open laboratories and strong educational districts.
+
+## Gameplay
+
+- mapping;
+- sample and evidence chains;
+- field bases;
+- discovery politics;
+- protecting fragile ecosystems;
+- choosing when exploration becomes settlement;
+- rescuing earlier expeditions.
+
+# 8. Bastion Escort Carrier
+
+## Character
+
+A fortified carrier used to protect convoys, evacuate populations and coordinate dangerous passages.
+
+## Multirole baseline
+
+Security does not replace:
+
+- care;
+- habitation;
+- repair;
+- logistics;
+- education;
+- rescue;
+- diplomacy;
+- public accountability.
+
+## Variants
+
+### Civilian convoy guardian
+
+Heavy rescue, warning and interception with restrained weapons.
+
+### Blockade runner support carrier
+
+Stealth, repair, medicine and cargo transfer.
+
+### Evacuation bastion
+
+Shelter, transport and humanitarian capacity.
+
+### Fleet command carrier
+
+Coordination and logistics with stronger combat capability and political risk.
+
+## Gameplay
+
+- escort planning;
+- sensor and information warfare;
+- rescue under fire;
+- rules of engagement;
+- evacuation;
+- repairing damaged civilian craft;
+- legitimacy after force is used.
+
+# 9. Carnival Exchange Carrier
+
+## Character
+
+A moving market, performance culture, diplomatic commons and fabrication hub.
+
+## Multirole baseline
+
+It still maintains clinics, logistics, repair, schools, gardens, rescue and defense.
+
+## Variants
+
+### Migratory market carrier
+
+Strong trade, guest docking and small-business fabrication.
+
+### Festival carrier
+
+Performance, hospitality, transport and temporary settlement deployment.
+
+### Diplomatic exchange carrier
+
+Translation, neutral meeting spaces and cultural archives.
+
+### Education and apprenticeship carrier
+
+Travels between regions carrying teachers, workshops and exhibitions.
+
+## Gameplay
+
+- markets;
+- cultural exchange;
+- performances;
+- contracts;
+- customs and smuggling;
+- guest politics;
+- festival deployment;
+- memes and folklore crossing between worlds.
+
+# 10. Night Burrow Carrier
+
+## Character
+
+A deep-hull carrier for Black Worlds and environments where exposure is repeatedly lethal.
+
+## Multirole baseline
+
+It includes care, research, fabrication, habitation, ecological support, deployment, education, rescue and governance rather than functioning only as an armored troop ship.
+
+## Variants
+
+### Radiation refuge carrier
+
+Shielded neighborhoods and continuity archives.
+
+### Cave and subsurface carrier
+
+Burrowers, geological labs and deployable shelters.
+
+### Acid-sea and toxic-atmosphere carrier
+
+Sealed ocean and atmospheric interface systems.
+
+### Horror-expedition support carrier
+
+Rescue, quarantine, redundant communications and evidence recovery.
+
+## Gameplay
+
+- hostile-world footholds;
+- limited deployment windows;
+- infrastructure under pressure;
+- co-op survival;
+- extraction and rescue;
+- crew psychology;
+- learning an alien environment rather than conquering it.
+
+# 11. Seed Ark Carrier
+
+## Character
+
+A civilization continuity vessel intended to carry people, ecologies, institutions and adaptable mobile bases across deep time.
+
+## Multirole baseline
+
+The seed mission demands broad capability by definition:
+
+- fabrication;
+- ecology;
+- medicine;
+- education;
+- governance;
+- exploration;
+- planetary interface;
+- trade and diplomacy;
+- rescue and defense;
+- archives and cultural life.
+
+## Variants
+
+### Generation ark
+
+Large lived population and long political history.
+
+### Embryonic or archive ark
+
+Smaller active population with greater stored continuity and ethical risk.
+
+### Distributed seed convoy
+
+Many ships share the mission, reducing single-point failure and increasing political complexity.
+
+### Atlas-enabled pioneer carrier
+
+Combines seed continuity with route establishment.
+
+## Gameplay
+
+- multi-generational life;
+- mission reinterpretation;
+- ecology;
+- education;
+- construction during travel;
+- arrival and settlement;
+- preserving or rejecting founder intent;
+- descendants transforming the original mobile-home lineage.
+
+# 12. Cross-Family Refit
+
+A ship can migrate between customary emphases.
+
+Examples:
+
+- a Bastion becomes a Mercy carrier after war;
+- a Forge becomes a Hearth carrier when workers bring families;
+- a Survey carrier becomes a Seed Ark after discovering a viable world;
+- an Ocean Bastion becomes a Carnival Exchange carrier among archipelagos;
+- a failed Gate Tender becomes a stationary nexus city;
+- a Night Burrow becomes a public refuge and school.
+
+Identity continuity should survive mission change.
+
+# 13. Build Variety Rules
+
+For every carrier family, author at least:
+
+- three hull-lineage combinations;
+- three ownership models;
+- four carried-base mixes;
+- three age states;
+- three cultural interior expressions;
+- two failure configurations;
+- one alien or posthuman interpretation;
+- one unexpected secondary-emphasis build.
+
+This creates variety through combinations rather than endless disconnected classes.
+
+# 14. Player Design Prompts
+
+When building or refitting, ask:
+
+- What must this carrier always be able to do?
+- What will it emphasize on this voyage?
+- What smaller homes must it carry?
+- Which worlds must it enter?
+- Who owns the docks and modules?
+- Where do ordinary residents live?
+- What happens when the primary mission fails?
+- Which capability is intentionally modest?
+- What old component must remain?
+- How will another society recognize it from far away?
+
+## Atlas Maxim
+
+> **A family gives the carrier a recognizable way of solving many problems. A mission profile decides which problems receive the most room today.**
